put:
  operationId: updateTimeOffPolicy
  x-verification-status: LIVE-VERIFIED
  x-evidence:
    - PROBE-LOG/20260521-060000-put.workspaces.time-off.policies-official-live-verified.json
  x-notes: |
    Full-replacement PUT for a time-off policy. Tool does GET-then-merge before
    PUT so unspecified fields are preserved (partial-update ergonomics over a
    full-replacement wire call). Official spec uses path param 'id'; our spec
    uses 'policyId' -- cosmetic, same URL segment.
    IMPORTANT: the existing TRUTH 'patch:' entry for this path (iter15
    LIVE-OVERRIDE) refers to PATCH /time-off/policies/{policyId} used by
    archiveTimeOffPolicy (Client.Patch with body {status: ARCHIVED|ACTIVE}).
    The update operation uses PUT (Client.Put with full merged body). Both
    verbs are accepted at the same URL path but serve distinct operations:
    PUT = field update (updateTimeOffPolicy), PATCH = status toggle
    (archiveTimeOffPolicy). The iter15 probe mislabeled the HTTP verb as PATCH
    because it was recorded at the spec-comparison level rather than confirmed
    at the wire level.
    Live probe: policy <redacted-id:084a4a18c0> PUT with same-name no-op
    confirmed HTTP 200, response includes full policy body with projectId,
    userGroupIds, userIds, approve object.
  x-truth-iter: iter22
  parameters:
    - {name: workspaceId, in: path, required: true, schema: {type: string}}
    - name: policyId
      in: path
      required: true
      description: Time-off policy ID. Official spec calls this 'id'; our spec uses 'policyId'.
      schema:
        type: string
  requestBody:
    required: true
    content:
      application/json:
        schema:
          type: object
          required: [name]
          properties:
            name: {type: string, maxLength: 150}
            timeUnit: {type: string, enum: [DAYS, HOURS]}
            automaticAccrual:
              type: object
              nullable: true
              properties:
                amount: {type: number}
                period: {type: string, example: YEAR}
                timeUnit: {type: string, enum: [DAYS, HOURS]}
            allowNegativeBalance: {type: boolean}
            approve:
              type: object
              properties:
                requiresApproval: {type: boolean}
                specificMembers: {type: boolean}
                teamManagers: {type: boolean}
                userIds: {type: array, items: {type: string}}
            everyoneIncludingNew: {type: boolean}
  responses:
    '200':
      description: Updated time-off policy -- full object
      content:
        application/json:
          schema:
            type: object
            properties:
              id: {type: string}
              name: {type: string}
              timeUnit: {type: string, enum: [DAYS, HOURS]}
              archived: {type: boolean}
              allowHalfDay: {type: boolean}
              allowNegativeBalance: {type: boolean}
              approve: {type: object}
              automaticAccrual: {type: object, nullable: true}
              automaticTimeEntryCreation: {type: object, nullable: true}
              everyoneIncludingNew: {type: boolean}
              negativeBalance: {type: object, nullable: true}
              projectId: {type: string, nullable: true}
              userGroupIds: {type: array, items: {type: string}}
              userIds: {type: array, items: {type: string}}
              workspaceId: {type: string}
